From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:54:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Single process: no crash on cross-origin isolation or a
 dialog's light dismiss

A page that asks to be cross-origin isolated (COOP same-origin with COEP
require-corp; WhatsApp Web) is, in Firefox, loaded into a new process with a
new browsing context: a context can never become isolated in place, CanSet
refuses, and a refused transaction is a deliberate crash. In one process
the load reuses the tab's context, so opening WhatsApp Web crashed the
browser every time. The change is left out: the page loads, not isolated.

Closing a <dialog> by tapping outside it (light dismiss) consumes the
history activation, which tells the other processes through ContentChild;
in one process there is none, and it crashed on null. Only the local
processes' contexts are updated there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp |  9 +++++++++
 dom/base/Document.cpp           | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp b/docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp
index 77b3e1c21f..b531e06b0e 100644
--- a/docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp
+++ b/docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp
@@ -700,8 +700,17 @@ void WindowContext::ConsumeHistoryActivation() {
   // including for example cross-origin iframes. As such we need to send an
   // message over the IPC boundary to ensure out of processes contexts also
   // consume their activations.
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+  // In a single process there are no other processes to tell, and no
+  // ContentChild to tell them with: closing a <dialog> by tapping outside it
+  // (light dismiss) got here and crashed on a null ContentChild.
+  if (XRE_IsContentProcess()) {
+    ContentChild::GetSingleton()->SendConsumeHistoryActivation(top);
+  }
+#else
   MOZ_ASSERT(XRE_IsContentProcess());
   ContentChild::GetSingleton()->SendConsumeHistoryActivation(top);
+#endif
 
   // Update the local process children immediately.
   top->ConsumeHistoryActivation();
diff --git a/dom/base/Document.cpp b/dom/base/Document.cpp
index 9602541b0c..a7267b1d45 100644
--- a/dom/base/Document.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/Document.cpp
@@ -3553,6 +3553,10 @@ bool Document::IsCallerChromeOrAddon(JSContext* aCx, JSObject* aObject) {
                        principal->GetIsAddonOrExpandedAddonPrincipal());
 }
 
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+extern "C" void GeckoW10mNote(const char* aText);
+#endif
+
 static void CheckIsBadPolicy(nsILoadInfo::CrossOriginOpenerPolicy aPolicy,
                              BrowsingContext* aContext, nsIChannel* aChannel) {
 #if defined(NIGHTLY_BUILD)
@@ -3716,6 +3720,29 @@ nsresult Document::StartDocumentLoad(const char* aCommand, nsIChannel* aChannel,
       docShell->GetBrowsingContext()) {
     CheckIsBadPolicy(policy, docShell->GetBrowsingContext(), aChannel);
 
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+    // A page that asks to be cross-origin isolated (COOP same-origin with
+    // COEP require-corp: WhatsApp Web does) gets, in Firefox, a new process
+    // and with it a new browsing context, because a context can never
+    // become isolated, nor stop being, in place: CanSet refuses, and a
+    // refused transaction is a deliberate crash. This port runs in one
+    // process, so the load reuses the tab's context and WhatsApp Web
+    // crashed the browser every time it was opened. The change is left
+    // out instead: the page loads, just not isolated (no
+    // SharedArrayBuffer), as in a browser without the feature.
+    {
+      const auto requireCORP =
+          nsILoadInfo::OPENER_POLICY_SAME_ORIGIN_EMBEDDER_POLICY_REQUIRE_CORP;
+      const auto current = docShell->GetBrowsingContext()->GetOpenerPolicy();
+      if (current != policy &&
+          (current == requireCORP || policy == requireCORP)) {
+        GeckoW10mNote(
+            "document: a page asked for cross-origin isolation; one process "
+            "cannot give it a new browsing context, so it loads without");
+        policy = current;
+      }
+    }
+#endif
     // Setting the opener policy on a discarded context has no effect.
     (void)docShell->GetBrowsingContext()->SetOpenerPolicy(policy);
   }
